Z||000000||dreams||05-14-2001||10:16 PM||||I have an 84 and its exhaust manifold turns bright red and it is ideling high. If I adjust the timing it stalls. All the sensors seem good, I have replaced many of them and it still is doing it. Any ideas?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Formula88||05-14-2001||10:27 PM||||Clogged catalytic converter or other exhaust restriction.  My 88 Formula just started doing that and the exhaust sounds like you're blowing through a straw.  Gotta pull the exhaust loose to make sure.  Also inspect for kinked pipes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||05-14-2001||10:28 PM||||Just a few stabs.  IF your ses light is not on the computer thinks it is running normally.  So the problem could be a fault throttle position sensor. or. seized idle air control valve. or. a vacume leak, from a vacume hose problem or throttle body/intake gasket sucked in.  ??????  could even be a temp sensor reading -35 and is on high idle.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||05-15-2001||01:16 AM||||Is the timing mark on your harmonic balancer accurate?  If the balancer gets messed up (the outer spins on the inner) then the mark will be messed up.  Take #1 plug out, use a straw and see if TDC is close to a non-moving straw.  How many mi on the car?||||reg||1
